* `wdcaltdigin` (in work) -- *"wdc alt-ctrl: a READ of the Drive Address register returns the alt-status byte, which
  matches no hardware on any layout"*; its detector is the one wdc probe gate 10 runs in a single-leg `GATE` mode (S16).
* `wdcaltoffleg` (open) -- *"The THREE altoffset WDC differentials as ONE instrument -- wdc_altoffset_probe.py and the two
  that `import wdc_altoffset_probe as W' (_sig, _4bit): ..."*; it OWES those probes an exit status and a single-leg form
  (S16).
* `wdcaltfixture` (open) -- *"wdcaltfixture  every alt-ctrl row runs in a state NO REAL DRIVER IS EVER IN, so eleven
  single-field qualifications escape the whole file"*; its exemplar is the `&& !d->lba` qualification (P17).
* `arcpartlba` -- **NOT a ledger row.**  `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md` 24253 (VERBATIM): *"* 2730-2731 -> `arcpartlba` (named in
  this file only: no ledger row of its own)"*; 23432 lists it as a member of the class row `astraretrolow`: *"`arcpartlba`
  -- OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:2730-2731 at db8b1a33 -- the ARC partition LBA is multiplied by 512 in signed int and overflows
  (arcbios.c:1010-1017; it defeats the #168 bound)"*.  It is the same arithmetic class as the disabled LBA formula's
  `512 * (int)` product (S6, P8).

