## 3. The design and its sources -- and where they differ

**3.1 The main loop's design**, as handed to this drafter (`DRAFTER_INPUTS.md` 33-54; the coordinator's text, not a
repository record):
*`C:/Users/User00/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--DocumentNoSnc-cc-GXEMUL/8e474f41-4d47-4c99-bf11-3406a84c4fcd/scratchpad/t4/DRAFTER_INPUTS.md`, lines 33-54:*
~~~~
33| ## The design the brief puts to the panel (state premises as questions; ratification is not wanted)
34| 
35| 1. THE REPAIR: (a) decode the LBA flag from bit 6 (`WDSD_LBA` 0x40) and keep the SDH readback byte-exact (bits 7 and 5 are
36|    obsolete always-1 bits in ATA; the model's `sectorsize` field is the pre-ATA WD1003 reading of bits 7-6 -- is it read anywhere
37|    else?  grep); (b) enable the LBA28 formula at BOTH address sites (`((head & 0xf) << 24) + (cyl << 8) + sector`, 0-based sector);
38|    (c) IDENTIFY word 49: the research ruling says decide it FIRST.  Main-loop position to be refuted: KEEP word 49 = 0 in this
39|    round (every rig's guest would otherwise switch from CHS to LBA addressing -- a guest-visible behaviour change on five rigs that
40|    needs its own measured warrant), and FILE the advertisement as a follow-up whose gate is the five-rig boot battery.  Is a guest
41|    that ignores word 49 (the research names FreeBSD 10+) the only beneficiary, and is that enough?  What must NOT change: the CHS
42|    formula, drive/head decode, the ATAPI path, `#481`'s control-register handling, the `wdc_altstatus` region.
43| 2. THE DETECTOR (`regress/wdc_lba_probe.py`, two legs in one invocation like `wdc_altoffset_probe.py`): the floor enumerated from
44|    the fix's predicates and body-read lvalues (`lba`, `head & 0xf`, `cyl`, `sector`, the write path vs the read path); the accept
45|    side (CHS requests still land where they did: rows `chs s1`/`chs s2`/`chs h1`; readback byte-exact: `sdh rb`/`sdh rb2`);
46|    the anchor rule (a tag per sector is an anchored oracle); the clause-(c) null medium (an executable non-emulator, since the gate's
47|    `need_exec` turns an absent binary into SKIP); the dead-run score to be MEASURED; variants to enumerate: bit-5 decode reinstated,
48|    `& 0xf` dropped (needs LBA >= 2^24 -- disclose), `<< 8` wrong, `sector - 1` in the LBA arm, LBA formula applied to CHS too,
49|    one site fixed and the other not; the gate home (grep `regress/gate_*.sh` for `wdc_altoffset_probe` and put this probe beside
50|    it); the `check_probe_wiring.py` class line.
51| 3. FILINGS / RECORDS: the word-49 follow-up row (if kept at 0); any LBA48 note (`0x24`/`0x34` commands -- out of scope, say so);
52|    the ledger `witness` term (`probe:<path>` with the witness artifacts if the base leg is measured red on the committed build
53|    BEFORE the fix edit -- the oracle-correction order rule -- else `detector:<path>`); what the CHANGELOG block must and must not
54|    claim (it must not claim guests now use LBA; it must say word 49 is unchanged).
~~~~

**3.2 The research's fix** is B's recommendation 1 (1.5): decode bit 6; compute
`((head&0xf)<<24)|(cyl_hi<<16)|(cyl_lo<<8)|sector` at both sites; keep the SDH readback byte-exact; keep word 49 = 0.

**3.3 The adjudication** is `ADJ_RULINGS.md` B and D (1.3): file as latent; decide word 49 FIRST; do not port the patch.

**3.4 The FreeBSD / DragonFly patch** (`distro_patches/freebsd_ports/files/patch-src_devices_dev__wdc.c`, whole file,
VERBATIM; the DragonFly DPorts copy is byte-identical, `cmp` at drafting).  Its hunk offsets (274, 320) are upstream 0.7.0's
line numbers, not this fork's:
*`regress/artifacts/research_20261022/distro_patches/freebsd_ports/files/patch-src_devices_dev__wdc.c` at HEAD, lines 1-30:*
~~~~
