1510|         #  denominator cannot tell a probe that LOST rows from one that never had
1511|         #  them -- which is this file's own padded-column lesson one level up.
1512|         #  *** PIN MOVED 16 -> 19 ON 2026-09-11 (#525 pass 2), DELIBERATELY. ***  The
1513|         #  probe gained a three-row phase that drives the offset-1 decline with DRDY
1514|         #  CLEAR, by selecting the ABSENT SLAVE (0xb0 -> wd_sdh).  Without it the
1515|         #  one-token mutant `if (odata & WDCS_DRDY) odata = 0;` swept all 16 rows:
1516|         #  every earlier row drives DRDY SET (0x51 / 0x58), so the mutant zeroed
1517|         #  anyway and was invisible BY CONSTRUCTION.  A pin that follows the probe
1518|         #  cannot tell a probe that GAINED rows from one that LOST them, which is
1519|         #  why the literal moves by hand and says why.
1520|         #  PIN 19 -> 22 (2026-09-12, #525 pass 3): the 0x01 cell (absent slave at
1521|         #  power-on) and the 0x50 cell (post-SRST), closing the status-bit class.
1522|         check "wdc_altdigin rows run"     "${adres#*/}" 22
1523|         check "wdc_altdigin rows correct" "${adres%/*}" "${adres#*/}"
1524|     fi
1525| fi
