*`tools/BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md` (working tree), lines 636-650:*
~~~~
636| Any brief for a round that ships or extends a detector states clause (c) in one of these two forms -- never as a
637| bare clause letter beside a row name, and never by pointing at the `[IDENTITY]` self-count row (that is E1 hygiene):
638| 
639| ```
640| (c): measured at <artifact>                                  -- the null-medium leg was run; its receipt is durable
641| (c): by construction via <row/pin>, leg not run              -- checked by READING the shape named
642| ```
643| 
644| **The null medium by instrument kind** (one criterion: a product medium carrying none of the behaviour under test):
645| an offline differential that `#include`s the product -> a COMMENT-ONLY product source that fails to compile under a
646| gate that reds on the compile failure; a runtime probe -> an absent or non-emulator binary, or a build without the
647| device; an instruction-handler round -> an IDENTITY BODY (decode and retire, write nothing).  **The pre-fix build is
648| clause (a)'s medium and never clause (c)'s.**  A by-construction claim fails its reading -- and the leg is owed --
649| when the probe has no runtime gate wiring, the gate pins with `check_min` or not at all, or the control is computed
650| over the row list (`all([])` is True).  Predict a dead run's score from the source (some rows test only exit status).
~~~~
* **R23 -- round scope:**
*`C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/CLAUDE.md`, lines 2877-2880:*
~~~~
2877| **Round scope (the reopening rule):** a witness makes a site ELIGIBLE, never mandatory. A round
2878| takes ONE site; a second joins only if it is witnessed, in the SAME device and SAME semantic class
2879| under the third doctrine arm (so one fix design covers both), and covered by the SAME detector
2880| with no new oracle. **More witnesses create more candidate ROUNDS, never bigger rounds.**
~~~~

