  1| """wdclbaaddr -- RUNG-3 WITNESS AND DETECTOR for the wdc LBA-mode address decode.
  2| 
  3| Real guest instructions, real address decode, real memory_rw, on an UNMODIFIED
  4| in-tree machine description (evbmips -e malta, whose committed piix4_ide path adds a
  5| wdc whenever an IDE image is attached).  Attaching a disk image with -d is ordinary
  6| operation, not a machine edit.
  7| 
  8| THE DEFECT (all in src/devices/dev_wdc.c at HEAD; durable keys are grep anchors):
  9| 
 10|     grep -n 'case wd_sdh:'        dev_wdc.c   -- SDH (taskfile offset 6) decodes the
 11|         lba flag from BIT 5 on write (`d->lba = (idata >> 5) & 1;`) and recomposes it
 12|         the same way on read (byte-exact: the four fields partition the byte).  ATA
 13|         puts the LBA flag in BIT 6 (0x40); bits 7 and 5 are the obsolete "always 1"
 14|         bits, so the CHS select byte is 0xa0 and the LBA select byte is 0xe0.  Under
 15|         the HEAD decode every 0xe0 is read as head=0, and d->lba is never consulted
 16|         for an address anyway:
 17|     grep -n 'void wdc__read'      dev_wdc.c   -- offset = 512 * (sector - 1 +
 18|         head*spt + heads*spt*cyl); the LBA28 alternative
 19|         512 * (((head & 0xf) << 24) + (cyl << 8) + sector) sits inside `#if 0`.
 20|     grep -n 'void wdc__write'     dev_wdc.c   -- the same CHS/LBA pair on the write
 21|         side.
 22|     grep -n '49: capabilities'    dev_wdc.c   -- IDENTIFY word 49 stays 0 this round
 23|         (LBA is not advertised); words 3 and 6 carry heads and spt.
 24| 
 25| So a command issued in LBA mode is served from the CHS interpretation of the same
 26| taskfile bytes.  The fix decodes lba from bit 6, keeps the readback byte-exact, and
 27| enables the LBA28 formula at both sites.
 28| 
 29| THE VEHICLE copies regress/wdc_altoffset_probe.py: the command line and disk prefix,
 30| the pty/expect debugger driver (print/breakpoint/continue idioms), the MIPS encoders
 31| (I, lui, ori, addiu, sb, lbu, beq, emit) plus lhu (opcode 0x25) and sh (opcode 0x29)
 32| added in the same style, the KSEG1 register addresses (0xb80001f0 + N: 0 data 16-bit,
 33| 2 seccnt, 3 sector, 4 cyl_lo, 5 cyl_hi, 6 SDH, 7 command/status), the per-instruction
 34| disassembly self-check, and the row/verdict/sentinel protocol.  malta is LITTLE-endian;
 35| the data port is read 16 bits at a time (lhu), 256 words per sector.  Every instruction
 36| is encoded from the field layout -- never a typed-in machine-code constant.
 37| 
 38| THE DISK IMAGE (4096 sectors of 512 bytes, generated under the output dir, never the
 39| repo):  sector n carries, as little-endian 16-bit words, word0 = n & 0xffff,
 40| word1 = (~n) & 0xffff, word2 = 0x4c42 ("LB"), word3 = 0x4100 ("A\\0"), rest zero.  The
 41| TAG of a sector is the pair (word0, word1) and is a DEVICE SIGNATURE: no RAM cell holds
 42| it, so a read that returns a tag proves the bytes came through the disk model.  The
 43| probe reads word0 and word1 and compares the combined value (word1 << 16) | word0.
 44| 
 45| THE ROWS (one fresh emulator process per session; H = IDENTIFY word 3, S = word 6):
 46| 
 47|     row            session   want on COMMITTED (HEAD)         want on FIXED
 48|     live ram       every     0x5a5a                           0x5a5a
 49|     id w49         identify  0x0000                            0x0000
 50|     id geo         identify  words 3,6 nonzero                 same
 51|     chs s1         chs       tag 0                             tag 0
 52|     chs s2         chs       tag 1                             tag 1

