*`regress/images.md` at HEAD, lines 130-157:*
~~~~
130| ## SuperH / landisk - the wdc scratch disk (`landiskdisk`)
131| 
132| **This one you generate; there is nothing to download.**
133| 
134| ```
135| cd _images
136| dd if=/dev/zero of=wdc-scratch-64m.img bs=1M count=64
137| ```
138| 
139| 64 MiB of zeros, 67,108,864 bytes exactly. `drive_guest.py` attaches it to the landisk
140| rig as `-d iR:<path>` when it is present, and boots exactly as before when it is not -
141| printing `RIG_DISK=0 absent:<path>` so the difference is visible in the log. **A silent
142| revert to zero wdc coverage would be indistinguishable from coverage that ran.**
143| 
144| ### Why it exists
145| 
146| Without it `dev_wdc.c` has **zero rig coverage in the entire battery**. The landisk rig
147| boots a ramdisk, so `wdc0` attaches and is never driven - measured: not one ATA opcode
148| reaches the command register across a full boot to the installer prompt. With the disk,
149| the same boot issues 14 command-register writes across seven opcodes.
150| 
151| ### Scope it honestly
152| 
153| It gives **zero coverage of `wdc_command()`'s `default:` arm**, which is where every
154| filed wdc defect lives - "Unimplemented command" warnings on a disked boot measured
155| **zero**. Its real value is `0xF5 SEC_FREEZE_LOCK` as `wdcnoirq`'s witness, plus general
156| wdc exercise. `0xE0`, `0x30 WRITE` and `0xC5 WRITEMULTI` need a full filesystem lifecycle
157| through `halt -p`, which this rig never performs.
~~~~

